---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const factors = [
  "Age of the vehicle",
  "Mileage or odometer reading",
  "Make, model, and brand popularity",
  "Mechanical and structural condition",
  "Service history and maintenance records",
  "Body condition and appearance",
  "Accident and repair history",
  "Vehicle usage: private or commercial",
  "Imported versus locally assembled status",
  "Spare-parts availability and maintenance cost",
  "Modifications and customisation quality",
  "Current market demand and seasonality"
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="Factors Affecting Car Valuation in Kenya | Unitech Accident Assessor"
  description="Discover the key factors that affect a vehicle's market value in Kenya, from age and mileage to condition and demand."
  pageTitle="Factors Affecting Car Valuation in Kenya"
>
  <main class="page-main">
    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="content-grid">
        <article class="article-card">
          <p class="article-lead">
            A car’s value in Kenya is shaped by more than make and model. Condition, usage,
            maintenance, accident history, and market demand all influence the final figure.
          </p>

          <h2>Key valuation factors</h2>
          <div class="factor-grid">
            {factors.map((factor) => <div class="mini-card">{factor}</div>)}
          </div>

          <h2>What valuers look for most closely</h2>
          <p>
            The biggest drivers of value tend to be age, mileage, mechanical condition, and
            whether there is evidence of accident damage or poor repairs. These can affect both
            resale value and what an insurer is willing to recognize.
          </p>

          <h2>Why market demand matters</h2>
          <p>
            Popular brands with reliable spare-parts support, such as many Toyota, Subaru, and
            Mazda models, often retain value better in Kenya. High fuel prices, rural demand for
            SUVs, and broader economic conditions can also shift pricing.
          </p>

          <h2>Why documentation supports value</h2>
          <p>
            A strong service history, consistent ownership details, and clear repair records help a
            valuer defend the figure given in the report. Missing or inconsistent records can lower
            buyer and insurer confidence.
          </p>
        </article>

        <aside class="sidebar-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Quick takeaway</p>
          <h2>Condition and proof matter.</h2>
          <p>
            Two vehicles of the same model year can have very different values depending on
            maintenance, accident history, and usage.
          </p>
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/services/pre-purchase-vehicle-valuation/">
            Book a pre-purchase check
          </a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
